# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# tools/mvlr's synthesized test-main driver for --backend=wasm (#2033) —
# written as a hidden sibling of the *_test.mvl source so mvl build's
# directory-relative sibling loader can still find it, cleaned up on exit.
.mvlr_synth.*

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
site/
AGENTS.md
!etc/AGENTS.md
*.jsonl
librust_out.rlib
*.profraw

# LLVM IR/bitcode — generated build artifacts
*.ll
*.bc

# WASM text output — `mvl build --backend=wasm` writes `<stem>.wat` into the
# working directory, so building an example in place leaves one behind.
# Scoped to examples/ rather than a blanket `*.wat`: the reference modules in
# tests/spikes/006-wasm-backend/ are checked in on purpose.
examples/**/*.wat

# Fuzzing runtime artifacts (cargo-fuzz)
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Python bytecache
**/__pycache__/

# Runtime database artifacts (crud_api example)
crud_api.db
examples/crud_api/crud_api.db

# Local project package directories (legacy; packages now resolved from XDG cache)
.mvl/

# Marimo notebook session data
tracker/
